}} |-|Explanations= {{#tag:tabber| -Pages= Goku-Ki-Kamehameha.png|Ki Manipulation|link=Ki Manipulation (Dragon Ball) DB Quilted multiverse owo.png|Dragon Ball Cosmology|link=Dragon Ball Cosmology -Blogs=}} |-|Notes={{Border|Scroll=Yes|Visible=No|Content=#Note 1: According to the Daizenshuu, Super Exciting Guide and Dragon Ball Z: Kakarot encyclopedia, Super Saiyan is officially a [https://imgur.com/a/super-saiyan-is-50x-multiplier-kuM7iGA 50x multiplier]. However, more than that, Super Saiyan is consistent with the showings in the manga as a 50x speed multiplier specifically. Goku using Kaioken x10 was being casually stomped by 50% Frieza, and even Kaioken x20 while using a Kamehameha was at best equal to 50% Frieza, yet using Super Saiyan allowed Goku to easily stomp 50% Frieza, and overpower 100% Frieza. Therefore, it is highly consistent with the 50x multiplier assigned to it. Similarly, Super Saiyan 2 and Super Saiyan 3 are [https://imgur.com/a/C8uBjX8 100x and 400x], respectively, as stated in the Super Exciting Guide, and more recently in Dragon Ball Z: Kakarot encyclopedia. Oozaru is officially a [https://imgur.com/a/D7aaOw6 10x multiplier] as stated directly in the source material and the Dragon Ball Super Exciting Guide as well. #Note 2: It has been stated numerous times across various sources in the series that a larger ki means greater statistics – statistics such as [https://imgur.com/tNJjg2h strength] and [https://imgur.com/ZBCGREl overall power], [https://imgur.com/NdBBzNO speed], [https://imgur.com/jgtiEmQ aerial capabilities], [https://imgur.com/Xf6sKDx destructive capacity], [https://imgur.com/a/KYhrxRq Goku also says to Toppo that SSG is his fourth transformation], and seeing how Super Saiyan 4 would be likely inferior he would have no reason to lie here. * Shin and Kibito remain fused at the start of Super, even though they unfused in Dragon Ball Daima which takes place before Super in the timeline. We are given no reason as to why this is the case, so it should be counted as a contradiction. [https://imgur.com/a/qg0fBPG And later when they unfused Goku is confused on how they were able to do it, even though an answer was already given with] Majin Buu in Daima, which predates Super. The fact that they went through the trouble of collecting the Namekian Dragon Balls instead of going to Majin Buu again is already weird to say the least. * Vegeta doesn't use Super Saiyan 3/Ultra Vegeta 1 against Beerus whatsoever even after breaking loose. The overall consensus is that Dragon Ball Daima has very dubious canon in relation to Super, and is thus treated as an alternate continuation of the original manga, rather than being part of the current overarching story. Furthermore, Dragon Ball Z: Kakarot is recognized as supplementary material to the original canon, as discussed in this thread. It's important to note that the gameplay and cutscenes of the game are not considered canonical to the original work due to contradictions and material from the TV anime that may not be faithful to the original manga. Therefore, only supplementary materials such as the game's encyclopedia would be considered valid for use. DLCs are not to be considered canon unless stated otherwise. |} {| class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" align="center" border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width:100%" | colspan="2" style="text-align: left; |Anime Canon |- | DBS Anime is also considered to continue from the events of DBZ Kai for the reasons that’ll be expounded upon below: * The DBS anime uses [https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=6oJMQe-FoVY scenes] [https://youtu.be/aDTgZDvTFKE from the DBZ Kai] [https://youtu.be/xSyzxDdzOGc anime] [https://youtu.be/ToktTPdGux8?si=qP_BUBjL8qeX6-T6 as character flashbacks] to represent events that took place in the previous arcs. These flashbacks also seem to show events that are anime-only, for example, during Trunks's flashback we see the Semi-Perfect Cell versus SS2 Gohan fight which is an anime-only battle and never took place in the manga, meaning the DBS anime follows the events of DBZ Kai anime rather than the Dragon Ball manga. * The presence of anime-only characters like [https://youtu.be/cifhvsSngqw?si=EbDDhiJ7K3VgjWhw Gregory] and [https://imgur.com/a/CtyTmLJ Mr. Satan's underlings] in the DBS anime who are absent from the Dragon Ball manga, even during important events such as during Cell's self-destruction on King Kai's planet, Gregory was nowhere to be found in the scene, indicating his absence in the manga's story, not to mention the official Dragon Ball website also calls him a "[https://dragon-ball-official.com/news/01_2736.html TV-series only character]" which is another proof of why the DBS anime should be canon to DBZ Kai. * Bulma [https://imgur.com/a/k1F7FP2 indicating] that the entire side story of Ginyu switching bodies with her happened in the past which is an anime-only story and isn't present in the manga, meaning that the DBS anime seems to follow events from DB
