{Nihongo|Princess Peach|ピーチ{{Ruby|姫|ひめ}}|Pīchi-Hime}} is a character in the critically acclaimed Super Mario series. In the series, she usually portrays the princess in distress and has been kidnapped by Bowser in almost every game. In the original game, she possessed strong white magic that would allow her to reverse the black magic of the Koopa clan, thus giving Bowser a reasonable answer to why he would kidnap the princess, as he was at the time using it to cast a spell on all of the Mushroom Kingdom's residents. The other reason of course, is that the Koopa King has, like many others, a crush on the mushroom-princess, as he expresses many times in the series Mario and Luigi, the protagonists of the series, always seem to rescue the princess and save the Mushroom Kingdom when needed. Other characters also lend a helping hand, such as Yoshi, Toad, Wario and a cast of other characters in the Mario RPGs. That being said, she does sometimes join Mario and the others on their adventures (Super Mario Bros. 2, Super Mario RPG: The Seven Stars, Super Paper Mario, Super Mario 3D World, Super Mario Run, Super Mario Bros. Wonder and both Mario Plus Rabbids games) and she even has her own two games (Super Princess Peach and Princess Peach: Showtime!) where she saves the day single-handedly. She also sometimes manages to help Mario when she is kidnapped by sending him useful information and power-ups or supports him with her magic. She is also a regular in the racing and sports spin-offs as well as the Super Smash Bros series since Melee. ==Powers and Stats
